    "summary": "Woodblock print, on hand-made paper probably from the daphne bush, of the type made for prayer-flags. Ink made of soot from an oil lamp.  In the centre is the &#039;wind horse&#039; carrying flaming jewels.  At the corners are the canonical Four Protective Animals (clockwise from top left) - garuda (with snakes), dragon, tiger and snow lion.  Between the images are invocatory texts in Tibetan and small auspicious symbols; at the top is the Banner of Victory.",
